  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 337 PM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\n===== Monday - Saturday =====\n\nBeginning Monday morning, we remain on the cool side of a surface \nhigh with a continued NE flow keeping highs in the mid to upper 80s. \nAs dry as the air mass will be, PoPs will remain near zero for the \nwhole CWA with near normal highs. Overall synoptic pattern changes \nslightly as an Omega pattern begins to break down some. The ridge in \nplace over the plains will begin to move south with more of a zonal \nflow setting up over our area through the week.\n\nAt the surface, high pressure at the surface will shift east, and a \nsoutheasterly to eventually southwesterly flow will return. Highs \nwill be boosted as a result into the 90s once again by Tuesday-\nWednesday. With the weakened ridge over the plains, a trough will \nmove through our area by later Wednesday and Thursday morning. A \nboundary will set up somewhere over the Ohio Valley acting as an \naxis for moisture to travel on. Rain chances mixed with storms \nreturns by then with slightly cooler highs in the mid to upper 80s. \nDepending on how far south the boundary pushes later in the week \nwill determine if highs remain in the 80s by Friday and Saturday or \nnot. For now, expect drier conditions to return by next weekend.",
